# Cursor environment baseline

Verified on this machine (2026-10-27):

- **Cursor** live **3.22.12** (`C:\Program Files\cursor\resources\app\package.json`). Latest Stable channel is **3.23.x** (installer staged at `target/live/cursor-setup-3.23.exe` — quit Cursor fully, then run it; in-app update on Windows often fails on leftover `_bak` locks). Leftover `Program Files\cursor\_bak` may still hold `chrome_200_percent.pak` (owner deferred wipe).
- **OpenCode** plugin **1.19.4** (`.opencode/` + `~/.config/opencode`); desktop app under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\@opencode-aidesktop`. Stay on 1.x unless the owner explicitly runs `opencode upgrade --major` for 2.x.
- **rustc / cargo** 1.92.0 (`1.92.0-x86_64-pc-windows-gnu`; `rust-toolchain.toml` names the gnu host). Do **not** export `RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN`. Host default stable may be newer (1.98+/1.99); only the pin builds this crate.
- **git** 2.50.0 (MSYS2 UCRT64)

## MCP / tools / sync (3.22+)

- Folder MCP only: [`.cursor/mcp.json`](../mcp.json) `type: http` + `url: http://127.0.0.1:9999/mcp` (Streamable HTTP to live `gsv-server`). Keep `type: http`. Do **not** write `streamable-http` — `cursor-agent` drops the whole `mcp.json` on that alias. Desktop **3.22.12** / **3.23.x** still uses this folder file (not User MCP).
- **Two agents online:** the IDE chat and the Agents Window can both be up. One writer on this tree (`S:\rust\GSV`). The second agent does not edit the same dirty files; parallel work is `/worktree` or cloud. Do not add a second MCP (User scope) so both windows “see” the hub.
- **Never** User MCP (`%USERPROFILE%/.cursor/mcp.json`) — it leaks `gsv_mcp_openbot` into PoolAI windows.
- **Hub rules in the rust environment:** `%USERPROFILE%/.cursor/hooks.json` `sessionStart` runs `gsv-cursor-rules` (`src/bin/gsv_cursor_rules.rs`). It inlines `AGENTS.md` + `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` only when a workspace root is under `S:/rust` and the hub folder itself is not already open. Folders outside that rust environment get nothing from the hook. A new Agent chat picks it up. Cloud agents do not run this user hook. `~/.cursor/rules` is not a global loader.
- Do **not** Origin-host this kit; GitHub `platinoff/GSV` stays the source of truth.
- Cursor **Projects** (cloud coordinator, Sep 2026) and cloud `/goal` swarms are **not** the VDT board. Drain stays `абракадабра` + GSV tickets + marshal-orchestrator on this box.
- Skills canon: [`.agents/skills/`](../../.agents/skills/). After skill edits: `cargo xtask mirrors`. Custom Mode (skill pinned with Alt+Enter) is optional; the drain skill stays Agent chat.
- Vision: `cargo xtask sync` then `cargo xtask sync --check`. MCP `gsv_xtask` `{task:sync}` is `--check` only; remirror is `gsv_vision_sync`.

## Drain settings

- Run Mode: **Auto-review** (not Run Everything). Steer: [`.cursor/permissions.json`](../permissions.json).
- Chat mode for `абракадабра` / `abrakadabra`: **Agent**. Plan only for ambiguous scope.
- Cursor Router Auto: **Balance** or **Intelligence** (not Cost) for long drain.
- Do not add project `sandbox.json` without OWNER (Windows VDT / MSYS2).

`GITHUB_TOKEN` / `ghs_*` — treat as **opaque** (may be JWT ~520). Do not length-check in CI/scripts.
